#{[17592186378678 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186378679 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378678 #edb/ref 1069 "q-135491" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378678 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378678 #edb/ref 1071 "In a particular town, the housekeepers use $2$ types of olive oil for preparing food: oil $A$ and oil $B.$  A study has shown that, each month \n\n- $40%$ of housekeepers who used oil $A$ swap to oil $B$, and\n\n- $30%$ of housekeepers who used oil $B$ swap to oil $A.$\n\nWhich of the following tables describes how these housekeepers change their preferences each month?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378678 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "df75b222-1f6c-5b44-9ba7-24d1998fa187" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378678 #edb/ref 1074 "We are given the following situation for each month: \n\n- $40%$ of housekeepers who used oil $A$ swap to oil $B.$ This implies that $60%$ of them remain using oil $A.$\n\n- $30%$ of housekeepers who used oil $B$ swap to oil $A.$ This implies that $70%$ of them remain using oil $B.$\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Oil $A$** | **Oil $B$** |\n| To: | **Oil $A$** | $0.6$ | $0.3$ |\n| **Oil $B$** | $0.4$ | $0.7$ |  |\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.4 & 0.7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186378679 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378679 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378679 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378679 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378679 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378684 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378679 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378679 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378679 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186378681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378679 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "81be96fa-a417-5d81-9fcf-9d833274bedd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378680 #edb/ref 1080 "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Oil $A$** | **Oil $B$** |\n| To: | **Oil $A$** | $0.4$ | $0.3$ |\n| **Oil $B$** | $0.6$ | $0.7$ |  |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378680 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378680 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c3ecc879-2c95-5f74-ac4a-ab969113e91a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378681 #edb/ref 1080 "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Oil $A$** | **Oil $B$** |\n| To: | **Oil $A$** | $0.6$ | $0.3$ |\n| **Oil $B$** | $0.4$ | $0.7$ |  |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378681 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378681 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c3a103d0-014c-5342-a350-b00b3703cd6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378682 #edb/ref 1080 "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Oil $A$** | **Oil $B$** |\n| To: | **Oil $A$** | $0.3$ | $0.6$ |\n| **Oil $B$** | $0.7$ | $0.4$ |  |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378682 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378682 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "778b5f63-aa15-579f-aa01-22ef9920862f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378683 #edb/ref 1080 "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Oil $A$** | **Oil $B$** |\n| To: | **Oil $A$** | $0.6$ | $0.7$ |\n| **Oil $B$** | $0.4$ | $0.3$ |  |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378683 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378683 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "11dc3d74-9a97-5c26-a835-b153e895787b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378684 #edb/ref 1080 "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Oil $A$** | **Oil $B$** |\n| To: | **Oil $A$** | $0.7$ | $0.6$ |\n| **Oil $B$** | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |  |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378684 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378684 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e109ecab-31bf-5d0c-a848-783e513a6076" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388382 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186388383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388382 #edb/ref 1069 "q-135446" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388382 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388382 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.35 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.65 & 0.7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{0}=\\begin{bmatrix}0.5 \\\\ 0.5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider a Markov chain with the stochastic matrix $P$ and the initial state vector ${x}_{0}$ given above. Calculate the state vector ${x}_{1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186388382 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0b120930-cc5f-5db6-89a1-4f05e7c988bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388382 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the state vector ${x}_{1},$ we apply one step of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.35 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.65 & 0.7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.5 \\\\ 0.5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.325 \\\\ 0.675\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186388383 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388383 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388383 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388386 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388383 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388387 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388383 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388388 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388383 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388383 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388383 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186388387 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388383 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "1799f441-3ae2-50b8-8266-618df3f86647" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388384 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}0.265 \\\\ 0.735\\